{"id": 538781944, "iid": 3963, "project_id": 34675721, "title": "chore: spec validation added", "description": "## Description\n<!--- Describe your changes in detail -->\n\n* chore: spec validation added\n\n## Summary\n\nBefore publishing a component to the GitLab catalog, the CLI now checks the component's spec file for common mistakes instead of blindly sending it to the server. Specifically, it verifies that the description isn't too long (max 256 characters), that any values listed under `component` are from the allowed set (`name`, `sha`, `version`, `reference`) with no duplicates, and that any ordering defined for inputs only references inputs that actually exist. If an unrecognized key is found in the spec, the tool issues a warning rather than failing outright, since the server has the final say on unknown fields. New tests cover all these validation scenarios.\n\n## Related Issues\n<!--- This project only accepts merge requests related to open issues -->\n<!--- If suggesting a new feature or change, please discuss it in an issue first -->\n<!--- If fixing a bug, there should be an issue describing it with steps to reproduce -->\nResolves #[issue_number]\n\n## How has this been tested?\n<!--- Please describe in detail how you tested your changes. -->\n<!--- Include details of your testing environment, and the tests you ran to -->\n<!--- see how your change affects other areas of the code, etc. -->\n\n## Screenshots (if appropriate):\n\n\nCloses #7699", "state": "opened", "created_at": "2026-09-26T00:15:49.225Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-26T00:38:00.176Z", "merged_by": null, "merge_user": null, "merged_at": null, "closed_by": null, "closed_at": null, "target_branch": "main", "source_branch": "7699-follow-up-validate-spec-for-components", "user_notes_count": 5, "upvotes": 0, "downvotes": 0, "author": {"id": 3507264, "username": "donaldcook", "public_email": "email-removed", "name": "Donald Cook", "state": "active", "locked": false, "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.